maluos-vault (0.4.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * first boot: the component waits up to 180 s for the restarted vault to
    answer and treats a socket timeout like a refused request; the compartment
    and token steps retry a transient timeout.  On a slow first boot one 30 s
    timeout escaped the health loop, the component failed, and the system
    compartment (mc2dbd-token, the API token, the BOS admin password) was never
    created.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:55:00 +0000

maluos-vault (0.4.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13 slice 1 (docs/phase13-slice1-nodes.md): a host principal
    (host:<hostname>, the node's identity in maluos-estate) may read the
    ledger's alert.% rows, which the node's report carries to the estate;
    everything else stays its own rows and its agents'.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:00:00 +0000

maluos-vault (0.4.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 12 slice 9. A grant request carries its cause: a broker (the
    gateway) passes what it was doing when the vault refused it (the model
    call: {call, model, backend, class, task, ts}; GET …/value?cause=JSON)
    and the request row keeps it (column maluos_secret_request.cause,
    detected at run time: hosts provisioned before 0.4.0 work without it).
    `maluctl secret requests` shows it.
  * Re-authentication before a reveal: GET …/value?reauth=polkit and
    POST …/rotate {"reauth": "polkit"} have the vault ask polkit whether
    the calling process may com.maluos.vault.reveal (auth_self: the
    person's own password through the session's agent; nothing is
    remembered). Refused: 401 reauth_required, ledgered; allowed: the
    ledger row carries detail.reauth = polkit. The polkit action file is
    shipped; without polkit (servers) the check refuses.
    `maluctl secret show|rotate --reauth`.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:06:51 +0000

maluos-vault (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Grant requests (Phase 12 slice 3): a refusal files a pending request
    for the secret's owner (table maluos_secret_request, one pending per
    secret and requester, asking again bumps it); GET /v1/requests,
    POST /v1/secrets/REF/request, POST /v1/requests/ID/approve|deny;
    `maluctl secret requests | request | approve | deny`. Approval makes
    the grant and records it on the request.
  * The agent registry maluos_agent (name, principal, owner) in the tenant
    schema, written by maluctl agent; a person's ledger view includes the
    rows of the agents they own.
  * Error bodies may carry extra fields (request_id on a refusal).

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000

